      "body": "fixes #64704\n\n### what changed\n`checkpoint_has_lm_head()` only inspected safetensors metadata. When loading pytorch `.bin` checkpoints with `tie_word_embeddings=True` where the checkpoint had an independent `lm_head.weight`, `checkpoint_has_lm_head()` returned `None`. This caused `maybe_untie_word_embeddings()` to exit early without untying, aliasing `lm_head` to `embed_tokens` and silently corrupting logits.\n\n- inspects `pytorch_model.bin.index.json` weight map via `get_hf_file_to_dict` when safetensors metadata is absent\n- inspects local/cached `pytorch_model.bin` on `meta` device with `torch.load(..., map_location=\"meta\", weights_only=True)` to avoid memory allocation\n- added unit tests covering sharded and single-file bin checkpoints in `test_config.py`",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "adenzhou1350"
            },
            "body": "Independently checked `4eeca134` (AI-assisted): your unchanged regression fails on parent `fac2ce2e` (`None is True` for the sharded index), then passes on your head — one test covering all five scenarios.\n\nI used Python 3.12.3 / Torch 2.14.0+cpu with the complete tracked Python trees and original project conftest/config. Older `e68efc685` CPU build artifacts were reused, so this is metadata-path validation, not an exact-head native rebuild or a rerun of full-model generation. The earlier generation control is in [#64704](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/issues/64704#issuecomment-6519604195).\n\nCommand: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/transformers_utils/test_config.py -k test_checkpoint_has_lm_head_pytorch_bin` (same new test applied to the parent for the failing control).",
